title: Main Opponent
subtitle: Whom our polemics address.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
card-image: img/poster_3.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.stanceAvailable(Q, 'main_opponent') !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card party.main_opponent (catalogue 4.2; technical reference 10.6): 1 T, 0 R, the card then waits 6 months. The present line is shown and cannot be
// chosen again; closing the card is free (Z — 0.32).
PolishParty.stanceView(Q, 'main_opponent');
!}

= Main Opponent

The present line: **[+ pl_stance_current +]**. A new declaration costs this month's action; it changes no law in force and gives no reform by itself.

- @nationalist_right
- @communists
- @capital_land
- @unconstitutional_force
- @easy_discard

@nationalist_right
title: The national right
subtitle: The addressee of polemics: ZLN.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.stanceStatus(Q, 'main_opponent', 'nationalist_right').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_stance_nationalist_right_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.stanceChoose(Q, 'main_opponent', 'nationalist_right');
!}
go-to: result

@communists
title: The communists
subtitle: The addressee: the KPP. Polemics cost −2 relation each and can close the way to contact.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.stanceStatus(Q, 'main_opponent', 'communists').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_stance_communists_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.stanceChoose(Q, 'main_opponent', 'communists');
!}
go-to: result

@capital_land
title: The defenders of capital and landed estates
subtitle: The addressees: the parties with land and fiscal ideals of −1 or less (in the test profile PSChD and ZLN).
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.stanceStatus(Q, 'main_opponent', 'capital_land').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_stance_capital_land_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.stanceChoose(Q, 'main_opponent', 'capital_land');
!}
go-to: result

@unconstitutional_force
title: Violence against the constitution, from any side
subtitle: The addressee: a party with an open case of unconstitutional violence; without one, polemics are blocked.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.stanceStatus(Q, 'main_opponent', 'unconstitutional_force').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_stance_unconstitutional_force_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.stanceChoose(Q, 'main_opponent', 'unconstitutional_force');
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

